content:
Looking at the crossings: at the right crossing, the strand from D continues smoothly (same direction of travel) onto the upper arc of the "lens." Following that upper arc across the top to the left crossing, it continues smoothly onto the tail heading down to A. The other pairings (e.g., D to B) would require a sharp turn at the crossing, i.e., switching curves.

Tracing: D → right crossing → upper arc → left crossing → A.

\boxed{A}
